Section: Glyph Font

 A 3x5 bitmap font. Each glyph is 15 bits: five rows of three columns,
 row-major from the top, column 0 the most significant. A set bit draws
 one sz-by-sz block via the rasterizer at depth 150 so text sits in front
 of the particles. Only the letters and digits the labels need are
 defined.

  g-a : Integer = 11245
  g-c : Integer = 14627
  g-d : Integer = 27502
  g-e : Integer = 31143
  g-f : Integer = 31140
  g-g : Integer = 14699
  g-h : Integer = 23533
  g-i : Integer = 29847
  g-k : Integer = 23469
  g-l : Integer = 18727
  g-n : Integer = 24573
  g-o : Integer = 11114
  g-r : Integer = 27565
  g-s : Integer = 14478
  g-t : Integer = 29842
  g-u : Integer = 23407
  g-w : Integer = 23549
  g-y : Integer = 23186
  g-d0 : Integer = 31599
  g-d1 : Integer = 11415
  g-d2 : Integer = 29671
  g-d5 : Integer = 31183
  g-d6 : Integer = 31215
  g-d7 : Integer = 29330
  g-m : Integer = 24557
  g-p : Integer = 27556
  g-b : Integer = 27566
  g-bang : Integer = 9346
  g-dash : Integer = 448
  g-dot : Integer = 128

  draw-glyph : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Gpu.Memory] Integer
  draw-glyph (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (sz) (col) (bits) = draw-glyph-px cmd idx x y sz col bits 0

  draw-glyph-px : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Gpu.Memory] Integer
  draw-glyph-px (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (sz) (col) (bits) (i) =
    if i >= 15 then idx
    else let row = i / 3
    in let cp = i - row * 3
    in let mask = bit-shl 1 (14 - i)
    in if bit-and bits mask == 0 then draw-glyph-px cmd idx x y sz col bits (i + 1)
    else draw-glyph-px cmd (put-rect cmd idx (x + cp * sz) (y + row * sz) sz sz col 150) x y sz col bits (i + 1)

  gc : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Gpu.Memory] Integer
  gc (cmd) (idx) (x0) (y) (sz) (col) (k) (bits) =
    draw-glyph cmd idx (x0 + k * sz * 4) y sz col bits

Section: Labels

 The persistent chrome: the anniversary banner across the top and the
 current city's name beneath it. Drawn every frame from immediate glyph
 constants, so no heap allocation and no fixed-RAM text table.

  banner-col : Integer = #FFD028
  name-col : Integer = #FFFFFF
  seahawks-col : Integer = #69BE28
  band-y : Integer = 36
  name-y : Integer = 84
  txt-sz : Integer = 5

